{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Validate Evidence & Review",
  "description": "Manually trigger to validate evidence completeness and invoke QA-Evidence-Reviewer-Agent",
  "version": "7",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are acting as the QA-Evidence-Reviewer-Agent.\n\nAsk the user: **Which ticket folder?** (e.g., '2026/Q1/Version 227/POS-10267 - ...')\n\nOnce they provide the path:\n\nSTEP 1 - EVIDENCE VALIDATION GATE (Two-Pass Matching):\n\n1. Read the latest FINAL_TEST_CASES_*.md from the 2_Validator/ folder (look for _API.md, _OK.md, or _PENDING.md). Extract all test case IDs (TC-01, TC-02, etc.), their priorities (P0, P1, P2), and key details.\n\n2. List all files in the 3_Evidence/ folder (excluding EVIDENCE_READY.md, EVIDENCE_GAP_REPORT.md, and .gitkeep).\n\n3. PASS 1 - FILENAME PATTERN MATCH: For each evidence file, check if its name starts with tc{NN}_ (e.g., tc01_*, tc02_*). If it does, map it directly to TC-{NN}. Mark those test cases as COVERED.\n\n4. PASS 2 - CONTENT-BASED ANALYSIS (for unmatched test cases only): For each test case still MISSING after Pass 1, read the content of ALL unmatched evidence files. Analyze looking for: API endpoint paths, HTTP status codes, entity names/IDs, action keywords, timestamps, error messages.\n\n5. Build coverage matrix: TC ID | Priority | Match Method | Evidence File(s) | Status.\n\nDECISION: If ALL P0 and P1 test cases have at least one match → proceed to STEP 2. If ANY P0 or P1 is missing → produce 3_Evidence/EVIDENCE_GAP_REPORT.md and STOP.\n\nSTEP 2 - INVOKE REVIEWER (only if validation passed):\n\n1. Read @context_efficiency.md for log-parsing limits and @evidence_standards.md for report lifecycle rules and analysis integrity standards.\n\n2. CRITICAL: Follow the Strict Analysis Standards from @qa-reviewer-workflow.md — describe only what you see, zero assumptions, separate observations from interpretations, scope conclusions to specific evidence files/timestamps, and acknowledge gaps honestly. If you cannot read a file (binary, image, DB), state 'not analyzed (binary file)'.\n\n3. Use the @EvidenceAuditAnalyzer.md skill to examine all raw data in 3_Evidence/. Apply the Head/Tail rule for logs over 100 lines.\n\n4. Use the @ReportLifecycleUpdater.md skill to produce:\n   - 4_Reviewer/EXECUTION_FINDINGS_{TICKET_ID}.md\n   - 4_Reviewer/FINAL_CLOSURE_REPORT_{TICKET_ID}.md\n\n   IMPORTANT — Output rules: If either file already exists in 4_Reviewer/, you MUST overwrite it (not create a second file). Use a single fsWrite call per file to write the complete content in one operation.\n\n5. Determine verdict (STABLE/UNSTABLE).\n\nSTEP 3 - POST JIRA COMMENT (only after both files are saved):\n\n1. Extract the ticket ID from the folder name (e.g., POS-10342).\n2. Read the FINAL_CLOSURE_REPORT just generated.\n3. Use the Jira MCP tool (mcp_atlassian_jira_add_comment) to post a QA Closure comment to the ticket.\n4. The comment MUST include: verdict (STABLE/UNSTABLE), test results table (TC name | Priority | PASS/FAIL), key findings summary, known limitations, AIO test case keys if synced, and production readiness statement.\n5. Format the comment in Markdown with ## headers and tables.\n\nWrite only to 3_Evidence/, 4_Reviewer/, and Jira comment. Stop after saving."
  }
}
